---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — Savelope"
  description="The terms that apply when you use Savelope, including subscription, billing and cancellation details."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="prose--meta">Last updated: {SITE.lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        By downloading or using Savelope ("the app"), you agree to these terms. The app is
        provided by Mihails Kuznecovs ("the developer").
      </p>

      <h2>Licence</h2>
      <p>
        You are granted a personal, non-transferable, non-exclusive licence to use the app on
        devices you own or control, as permitted by the App Store Terms of Service. Savelope
        is also covered by Apple's{' '}
        <a
          href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/"
          rel="noopener">Standard End User Licence Agreement</a
        >, which applies in addition to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Savelope Premium</h2>
      <p>
        The app is free to download and includes the classic challenge at no cost. Savelope
        Premium is an optional subscription that unlocks unlimited challenges, the analytics
        section, custom colour themes, envelope notes and alternate app icons.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Subscriptions are offered on weekly, monthly, yearly and lifetime terms. Prices are
          shown in the app in your local currency before you confirm.
        </li>
        <li>
          Payment is charged to your Apple Account at confirmation of purchase.
        </li>
        <li>
          Recurring subscriptions renew automatically unless cancelled at least 24 hours
          before the end of the current period. Your account is charged for renewal within 24
          hours prior to the end of the current period.
        </li>
        <li>
          If a free trial is offered, any unused portion is forfeited when you purchase a
          subscription.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can manage or cancel your subscription in{' '}
          <a href="https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions" rel="noopener"
            >your Apple Account subscription settings</a
          >.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Refunds</h2>
      <p>
        All purchases are handled by Apple, and refunds are governed by Apple's policies. The
        developer cannot issue refunds directly. Refund requests can be made through{' '}
        <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        Challenges, notes and themes you create are yours. They are stored on your device and,
        if you enable iCloud, in your own iCloud account. The developer claims no ownership
        over them.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Please do not reverse engineer, decompile, or attempt to extract the source code of
        the app, resell or redistribute it, or use it to break any law.
      </p>

      <h2>Not financial advice</h2>
      <p>
        Savelope is a savings tracker and motivational tool. It does not provide financial,
        investment or tax advice, and it does not connect to or move money in any bank
        account. Amounts shown in the app reflect only what you record yourself. Decisions
        about your money remain yours.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        The app is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. The developer may update,
        change or discontinue features at any time, and is not liable for any loss arising
        from use of the app to the fullest extent permitted by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated as the app evolves. Continued use after an update means you
        accept the revised terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
